From 039e432c7730a12deeac7a368ed3e812c928c79e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toemmsen96 <147745097+Toemmsen96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:03:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] power: supply: Add SM5703 charger status driver

Add a power supply driver for the battery charger of the Silicon Mitus
SM5703 PMIC and instantiate it from the MFD core driver.

The driver only reports the charger state, it never writes to the chip
and leaves the charger configured as the bootloader set it up:

 - ONLINE/PRESENT: VBUS is valid (STATUS5 VBUSOK set, VBUSUVLO and
   VBUSOVP clear)
 - STATUS: discharging without VBUS, full when the charger reports
   charge done (STATUS3 DONE) or top-off without CHGON, charging while
   CHGON is set, not charging otherwise
 - CURRENT_MAX, CONSTANT_CHARGE_CURRENT and CONSTANT_CHARGE_VOLTAGE
   decoded from the input current limit (VBUSCNTL), fast charge current
   (CHGCNTL2) and battery regulation voltage (CHGCNTL3)

The register layout follows the Samsung downstream sm5703_charger driver.

The power supply is registered as supplying "sm5703-fuel-gauge", so the
battery driver can tell whether external power is present. The PMIC
interrupt line is not described in the device tree yet, so the status
registers are polled every five seconds and power_supply_changed() is
called when the online state or the charging status changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
